{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundError"},{"type":"text","value":" type is used to represent a not-found error in TanStack Router."}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type NotFoundError = {\n  global?: boolean\n  data?: any\n  throw?: boolean\n  routeId?: string\n  headers?: HeadersInit\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"notfounderror-properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NotFoundError properties"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundError"},{"type":"text","value":" object accepts/contains the following properties:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"global-property-deprecated-use-routeid-rootrouteid-instead","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"global"},{"type":"text","value":" property (⚠️ deprecated, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"routeId: rootRouteId"},{"type":"text","value":" instead)"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"default: false"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If true, the not-found error will be handled by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" of the root route instead of bubbling up from the route that threw it. This has the same behavior as importing the root route and calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RootRoute.notFound()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"data-property","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" property"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom data that is passed into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" when the not-found error is handled"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"throw-property","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throw"},{"type":"text","value":" property"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"default: false"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided, will throw the not-found object instead of returning it. This can be useful in places where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throwing"},{"type":"text","value":" in a function might cause it to have a return type of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never"},{"type":"text","value":". In that case, you can use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound({ throw: true })"},{"type":"text","value":" to throw the not-found object instead of returning it."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"routeid-property","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"routeId"},{"type":"text","value":" property"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ID of the route that will attempt to handle the not-found error. If the route does not have a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":", the error will bubble up to the parent route (and be handled by the root route if necessary). By default, TanStack Router will attempt to handle the not-found error with the route that threw it."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"headers-property","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" property"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HeadersInit"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HTTP headers to be included when the not-found error is handled on the server side."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"notfounderror-properties","text":"NotFoundError properties","level":2},{"id":"global-property-deprecated-use-routeid-rootrouteid-instead","text":"global property (⚠️ deprecated, use routeId: rootRouteId instead)","level":3},{"id":"data-property","text":"data property","level":3},{"id":"throw-property","text":"throw property","level":3},{"id":"routeid-property","text":"routeId property","level":3},{"id":"headers-property","text":"headers property","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `NotFoundError` type is used to represent a not-found error in TanStack Router.\n\n```tsx\nexport type NotFoundError = {\n  global?: boolean\n  data?: any\n  throw?: boolean\n  routeId?: string\n  headers?: HeadersInit\n}\n```\n\n## NotFoundError properties\n\nThe `NotFoundError` object accepts/contains the following properties:\n\n### `global` property (⚠️ deprecated, use `routeId: rootRouteId` instead)\n\n- Type: `boolean`\n- Optional - `default: false`\n- If true, the not-found error will be handled by the `notFoundComponent` of the root route instead of bubbling up from the route that threw it. This has the same behavior as importing the root route and calling `RootRoute.notFound()`.\n\n### `data` property\n\n- Type: `any`\n- Optional\n- Custom data that is passed into `notFoundComponent` when the not-found error is handled\n\n### `throw` property\n\n- Type: `boolean`\n- Optional - `default: false`\n- If provided, will throw the not-found object instead of returning it. This can be useful in places where `throwing` in a function might cause it to have a return type of `never`. In that case, you can use `notFound({ throw: true })` to throw the not-found object instead of returning it.\n\n### `routeId` property\n\n- Type: `string`\n- Optional\n- The ID of the route that will attempt to handle the not-found error. If the route does not have a `notFoundComponent`, the error will bubble up to the parent route (and be handled by the root route if necessary). By default, TanStack Router will attempt to handle the not-found error with the route that threw it.\n\n### `headers` property\n\n- Type: `HeadersInit`\n- Optional\n- HTTP headers to be included when the not-found error is handled on the server side.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: NotFoundErrorType\ntitle: NotFoundError\n---\n\nThe `NotFoundError` type is used to represent a not-found error in TanStack Router.\n\n```tsx\nexport type NotFoundError = {\n  global?: boolean\n  data?: any\n  throw?: boolean\n  routeId?: string\n  headers?: HeadersInit\n}\n```\n\n## NotFoundError properties\n\nThe `NotFoundError` object accepts/contains the following properties:\n\n### `global` property (⚠️ deprecated, use `routeId: rootRouteId` instead)\n\n- Type: `boolean`\n- Optional - `default: false`\n- If true, the not-found error will be handled by the `notFoundComponent` of the root route instead of bubbling up from the route that threw it. This has the same behavior as importing the root route and calling `RootRoute.notFound()`.\n\n### `data` property\n\n- Type: `any`\n- Optional\n- Custom data that is passed into `notFoundComponent` when the not-found error is handled\n\n### `throw` property\n\n- Type: `boolean`\n- Optional - `default: false`\n- If provided, will throw the not-found object instead of returning it. This can be useful in places where `throwing` in a function might cause it to have a return type of `never`. In that case, you can use `notFound({ throw: true })` to throw the not-found object instead of returning it.\n\n### `routeId` property\n\n- Type: `string`\n- Optional\n- The ID of the route that will attempt to handle the not-found error. If the route does not have a `notFoundComponent`, the error will bubble up to the parent route (and be handled by the root route if necessary). By default, TanStack Router will attempt to handle the not-found error with the route that threw it.\n\n### `headers` property\n\n- Type: `HeadersInit`\n- Optional\n- HTTP headers to be included when the not-found error is handled on the server side.\n"}
